  "question": {
    "text": "A spring mass system (mass <math><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo></math> spring constant <math><mi>k</mi></math> and natural length <math><mi>l</mi></math> ) rests in equilibrium on a horizontal disc. The free end of the spring is fixed at the centre of the disc. If the disc together with spring mass system rotates about it&#39;s axis with an angular velocity <math><mi>&#969;</mi><mo>,</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>m</mi><msup><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math> the relative change in the length of the spring is best given by the option:"
  },
